      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1914-01-24_WidnesExaminer_art0040" n="art0040">
        <head>OFFICIALS AND STEWARDS.</head>
        <p>OFFICIALS AND STEWARDS.</p>
        <p>The stewards were: Sir Gilbert Greenall, Mr. John Cason, Capt. G. R. Crosfield, Colonel B. Fairclough, Mr. F. Aylmer Frost and Mr. W. Peter Rylands. This annual ball is the outcome of the efforts of a ladies' committee, of which Lady Greenall is the president, and Mr. G. Ireland-Blackburne and Mr. J. E. Greenall the joint hon. secre- taries. The committee is composed of: The Mayoress, Mrs. P. Peacock; Mrs. H. R. Armitage, Mrs. Ziba Armitage, Mrs. Bailey, Lady Harmood Banner, Mrs. G. Ireland Black- burne, Mrs. A. S. Bleckly, Mrs. W. Bracecamp, Mrs. Broadbent, Mrs. Coghill, Mrs. Coxon, the Hon. Mrs. J. E. Cross, Mrs. George Dakin, Mrs. Edelsten, Mrs. John Fairclough, Mrs. Edward Fox, Mrs. F. Aylmer Frost, Mrs. Green, Mrs. Ifenry Greenall, Mrs. Hutton, Mrs. Long, 31-rs. Monks, Mrs. J. Charlton Parr, Mrs. 11. V. Pigot, Mrs. Henry Roberts, Mrs. W. Peter Rylands, Mrs. Stewart-Smith, Mrs. Watkin, Mrs. J. J. Whitley, the Hon. Mrs. Willis, and Mrs. Willis. The laying of the special floor and part of the decorating work had been carried out by Mr. Ralph Johnson, but a number of ladies had lent their aid.</p>
        <p>The Winmarleigh Cafe catered in their usual excellent style.</p>
      </div>
