        <p>members who had had the pleasures a reading the most interesting book. The Bible lesson, "The Scholars of Christ,"' was opened by the Vice-president in a very able way, likening "The School" into a model Adult School, with Christ at+ its head, with the dis- ciples, who were drawa from all classes of men, as its scholars. The aim was to show that no man was debarred from membership, and that the only disqualification was lack of sincerity and devotion. The object of His teaching was to commit it to lives that should in some mea- sure reproduce His life.</p>
