        <p>as slight disinfectors. bloderd re- stherrehac htedae proved this fallacious. (Applause.) it seems strange,continued the Professer, that I sliould have eorne to Warrington to speak about smoke. I think you ought to take at * motto—" Charity begins at home." Warriogtos has done more towards reducing the smokiness of England than any other town in the countrr (Hear, hear.) But, like the shoemaker's wife, who was the worst shod in the village, it bah done little for itsel2. Gas Stove Pioneers. Here you have in Warrington Fletcher, 'Russell's works, 'which. have been the pioneers in the production of gas fuel. I remember oiti Thomas Fletcher, and it was he who introduced gas stoves of superior pattern, which retail' caused the introdnetion of coal gas for domestic heating to be so largely taken up in London During the last *re or six years the enormors improvements that have taken place in PO stoves have .led to one-sixth of the whole of the chimneys in London ceasing to emit smoke. (Applause.) What you have done in bringing about 0* enormous and mareellous improvement in th* area of London, -where i million gas fires as' in use, is to give an increase in the sunshine of 70 to 93 hours in the course of a year. Sine* 1884 fogs have detained from 29 bad fogs to seven, and that has been entirely the work ef this much-abused Smoke Abatement Soviet,' ' (Applause.)</p>
        <p>NOT FANATICS. Mr- J. A. RANSOMS, in proposing • vote 43 thanks to the leeturer. hoped that in Warring' ton they would try to put their own house order. A change could be brought about with out putting a serious burden upon roanufac Curers.</p>
        <p>Alderman BimNicer seconded and said some ot the leading mannfacturers were entirely it the League in the matter of smoke abatement. The reformers were not fanatics; they vter• really men of common-sense principles, and if they were before their time they could not heir that. (Laughter and applause.) Ths vote was carried, as was a similar comPli; mput to On ,Chairman, on the resolution. 0' Alderman SitICTILORS7, seconded by Mrs. I'llogr TOW.</p>
