        <p>Tanners Entertained. The employes of Messrs. Arthur Wareing, tanners, were entertained to am excellent sup- per at the Central Hotel on Monday evening, when a large number were present. An excel- lent musical programme followed.</p>
        <p>Memos. for School Children. The Warrington Education Committee have fixed the year's holidays as follows :—Easter, lith April; Whitsuntide, 29th May; Walking DaY, ISt July; Mid-summer. 17th July; Mid- term. 30th October; and Christmas, ard DeeeMber.</p>
        <p>Warrington Market Prices. The prices on Wednesday were: Wheat,'4s. 4d. to 4e. 6d. per 701 b.; oats, 2s. 6d. to 2s. 8(1. per 4511).; wheat straw, 28s. per ton; oat straw, 30s. per ton; XX flour, 235. 3d. per 2401 b.; bran, Is. 3d. per 201 b. Wheat slightly easier, oats remain unchanged, with a fair demand.</p>
