        <p>Colonel of South Laneashires Retiring. The most important change in the commands of Lancashire regiments during' the year will Dnetlur in March, when Lioutenant-Colonel D. G. rendergast is due to retire from the command of the 2nd Battalion South Lancashire Regi- rile°, now stationed on Salisbury Plain. Major Wanless, who is at present with the lit Battalion, in India, will probably assume the commandership. •</p>
