        <p>inCon'dust Explosions Ono methode venting explosions of coal M dust is to place stone dust where it collects, thus forming a mixture that is uninflarnmable. This plan has been tried at the Altofts collieries. The stone dust is applied about once in six months. Miners' Safety:of preventing It is covered over the haulage way ails and dust-collecting projections, or, where the walls are smooth, is placed on boards at the sides of the roads or suspended from the roof. At one ° 7,00_ yards o.2l.lau.age roads seam, where nearly f and junctions were dressed, the first cost was an eighth of a penny per ton of coal raised, the cost at. the second and third dressings having been at less than half that rate. The stone dust necessary varies with the kind.of coal, but an amount equal to that .of the coal dust usually gives perfect safety.</p>
