      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1914-01-24_WidnesExaminer_art0225" n="art0225">
        <head>'ANGLING.</head>
        <p>'ANGLING.</p>
        <p>Warrington Workingmen's Associa- tion.</p>
        <p>N.A. CENTRE. The general meeting of the Warrington centre took place at headquarters, Gladstone Arms, last week. There was a fair muster of members. Mr. T. Singleton was elected chairman for the evening, in the absence of Mr. J. Osborne. The secretary's report of the year's working showed how the society had made rapid strides since 1911. The membership has increased, the waters have been added to, the finances are satisfactory, and prizes of £3O value are offered for two matches. The set board and specials amounted to ..C7 3s. This season they are anticipating greater things, and with an increase of members the first item is to improve the set prizes, and to start a reserve fund for stocking and purchas- ing fresh waters. The suceess of the year must again be put down to the credit of the patrons and vice-presidents, who so`kindly contribute to the society year after year. We are pleased to see these gentlemen taking a keener interest in the workings of the club. GOWY ROACH. Only a few members have visited the Gowy verymupot eso satisfactory.t di._tprle yi o ft to ir sxe us l.enon ter there,baitsto asats ycsaiebt xc. ph elucftp the atof dawiaret oemtwhuaesrs. tahnrgoluegryshhtahvoesenooswouc.ollected enough dattiTh jeaedb omru besteats results have not been</p>
        <p>THE BAY HORSE. Annual meeting to-night at 7.30. Prizes will be paid out, and election of officers will take place.</p>
        <p>HEADQUARTERS. Any member who has not yet received his prize-money may have it on applying to Mr. E. Brookes. The first night for contritiutions is Monday, January 26. Contributions will only be taken at the club-house. It has been brought to the notice of the offi- cials that certain persons are in the habit of fishing in the length of the Gowy rented by the Northernqinglers. Steps are to be taken to stop non-members from angling in the waters.</p>
        <p>THE OFFICIALS FOR 1914. The following are the officials elected to govern the Centre during 1914: • President, Mr. H. Mather; chairman, Mr. J. Osborne; treasurer, Mr. E. Brookes; secretary, Mr. A. Stout; assistant secretary, Mr. W.</p>
        <p>Bailey; chairman of committee, Mr. W. Elli- son; committee, Messrs. Cox, Clare, Dixon, Hen- shall, Hill, Moores, Sanson. Isherwood, Wales, Whitfield, and Yallon; executive council, Messrs. J. Cox, W. Ellison and R. Clare.</p>
      </div>
