      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1914-01-24_WidnesExaminer_art0241" n="art0241">
        <head>FORD</head>
        <p>FORD</p>
        <p>CARS</p>
        <p>In stock-5 Seater Touring Car £135, complete with 5 Lamps, etc., etc. Quick delivery all models. Demonstrations arranged. Apply to the SOLE AGENT: W. KNIGHT, Stockton Heath Garage. Tel. 63,</p>
        <p>fashion, and Rollins was fouled inside the al•ea. Devonald took the kick and placed it safely beyond the reach of Forber. The Juniors were next penned to their own lines, and St. John's were awarded a corner, which was not im- proved upon, and then Meachin missed the goal by inches with a low shot. Tickle scored a few minutes before the final whistle blew. Re- sult: Orford" St. John's, three goals; Widnes Juniors, one goal.</p>
        <p>BILLIARDS.</p>
        <p>WARRINGTON LEAGUE. First Division. JUNIOR LIBERALS v. JUNIOR CON- SERVATIVES. Played at Horeemarket-street. Result Junior Liberals. Junior Conservatives. Handicap 210 Handicap 76 N. Wilkinson H. Williams J. A. Houghton... 100 J. Williams D. Shepherd 56 T. Cooper H. A. Williams.... 58 R. Bloomfield L. McMullen lOO I,V Ray P. Mann A. Wallington</p>
        <p>837 787 Majority for Junior Liberals, 50.</p>
        <p>RYLANDS' v. SENIOR CONSERVATIVES. Played at Gorsey-lane. Result :-A- s Rylands'. Seniors. Handicap 70 Scratch T. Warhnrst J. Gleave R. Haskell lOO W. Ford G. Thomas J. Jeffery W. Langley E. Blackkdge H. Eyes</p>
        <p>594 742 Majority for Conservatives, 148.</p>
        <p>EMILLNUEL INSTITUTE v. WALKER'S</p>
        <p>SOCIAL. Played at Knutsford-road. Result:—</p>
        <p>_ • Walker's. Emmanuel. Handicap ;90 Handicap 220 S. Baird J. Dagnall J. Roach T. Clare A. Appleton J. Rigby M. Sloan F. Mumby 59 • W. Bibby</p>
        <p>889 813 Majority for Walker's, 75.</p>
        <p>ST. MARY'S C.Y.M.S. v. JUNIOR CON- SERVATIVES. Played at Buttermarket-street. Result:— Junior Conservatives. St. 'Mary's. Handicap 76 Handicap 160 J. Williams R. Bloomfield W. Ray T. Cooper J. Jolley 11. Lockett 55 F. Tivnan T. Gorton lOO L. Miller J. Bate</p>
        <p>809 739 Majority for Junior Conservatives, 70.</p>
        <p>JUNIOR LIBERALS v. SENIOR LIBERALS. Played at Horeemarket-street. Result : Junior Liberals. Senior Liberals. Handicap 210 Handicap 65 H. Williams D. Shepherd N. Wilkinson H. A. Williams.... 100 E. A. Sanders L. McMullen J. Houghton G. Mann • 100 Coun. Halliwell 94 E. 1 Wallington</p>
        <p>783 823 Majority for Senior Liberals, 40. Pariah Church, 907; Whiteeross, 896.</p>
        <p>Second Division. LEAGUE OF-THE CROSS v. JUNIOR CONSERVATIVES. Played at Bewsey-street. Result:— League of the Cross. Junior Conservatives. Handicap 90 Scratch I. Tracery F. Lloyd J. Donlan P. Leonard 7. Emmott J. Mannion B9 W. Clark 631 482 Majority for League of the Cross, 139. SENIOR CONSERVATIVES v. RYLANDS'. Played at Sankey-street. Result:— _ . _</p>
        <p>.Senior Conservatives. Rylands'. Scratch Handicap 46 F. Holland H. C. Simpson A. W. Allman D. Cotterill R. Anderton ........ 100 W. Whittle J. Allen</p>
