      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1914-01-24_WidnesExaminer_art0247" n="art0247">
        <head>CROSS COUN TRY.</head>
        <p>CROSS COUN TRY.</p>
        <p>• Warrington A.C. had 20 runners over an eight - mile col rse. J. Hanson, closely attended by C. Vose throughout, again emphasised the value of the international's coaching. E. Scott, in good style, maintained the splendid form he has pre- ,viously shown this season. A. Gregson is rapidly regaining,the form which earned for him last season the title of West Lancashire Junior Champion. J. Parsonage and W. Bolton dis- played signs that they are getting fitter. H. Holbrook and T. Turton, followed by H. Jepson and A. Burgess, came through at a steady gait. P. Antrobus brought F. Baker along nicely, the novice, following the international spiritedly. As a result of the run the senior points competi- tion now stands: 1, J. Hanson, 39; 2, C. VOl3O, 34; 3, E. Scott, 30; J. Parsonage and H. Hol- brook tie with 23 points each for the next posi- tion.</p>
        <p>To-day's Fixtures. rn addition to their novice, intermediate ant/ -</p>
        <p>_ senior competitions, Warrington A.C. run— off an inter-club race with Ithncoin who, although without several of their best runners. Put up a good fight with Crewe Harriers and Northwich at the latter's headquarters on Sat- urday. Meet at headquarters at 3.15 p.m. and finish at the bottom of Chester-road about 4.30.</p>
        <p>JOHN WALKPR AMID CO. LTD.,</p>
        <p>GENERAL AND ARTISTIC PRINTERS.</p>
        <p>BEWSEY STREET, WARRINGTON.</p>
      </div>
