        <p>RIFLE SHOOTING. APPLETON CLUB'S COMPETITION. The monthly competitions of the above dale terminated on Friday. Three competition* nave been in progress, all at 25 yards, unlimited entry. the possible score in each case being 100. Results:- Competition 1.-Ten shuts deliberate- First prize, silver-mounted dish; seoend prize, pair of vases-1, J. Hartley (first prize); 2, C. P. Day (second prize); 3, F. Tole; 4, A. Shepherd; 5, H. Baines; 6, F. Black; 7, J. Towers; a, J. W. Elliott; 9, W. Hutcheson; 10, P. Harrison; 11, F. J. Grocott; 13, F. C. Bennion ; 13, J. Allar- dice; 14, C. 'Jackson; 15, C. Shepley; 16, 11. Westmoreland; 17, R. Jackson; 18, R. W. R. Cook; 19, E. Lidiarel. Competition 2.-Ten shots rapid in 90 seconde at a green target. First prize, shaving stand;: second prize, metal cigarette box-1, A. Shep- herd (first prize); 2, S. James (second prize); 3, F. Tole; 4, C. P. Day; 5, H. Baines; 6, F. C. , Bennion ; •, J. Hartley; 8, W. Hutcheson; 9, It. Jackson; 10, F. Black; 11, F. J. Grocott; 12, H. Westmoreland; 13, R. W. B. Cook. Competition 3.-The aggregate scores of Com- petitions 1 and 2. A silver media', kindly pre- sented to the club by the Rhen West Explosive Co., makers of "R" ammunition-1, A. Shep- herd, medal; 2, S. James; 3. F. Tole; 4. C. P. Day; 5. IT. Baines; 6, F. C. Hennion ; 7, J. Ffart- • ley; 8, W. Hutcheson; 9, Y. Brack; 10, F. J. IGrocott; 11. R. Jackson; 12, H. Westmoreland; ' 13, R. W. B. Cook.</p>
